# Build artifacts
/bin/
/dist/
/genai-otel-bridge
/harness
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Generated license/SBOM artifacts (release-time: baked into the image at /licenses/ and
# attached to the GitHub Release — never committed; they churn on every dependency bump).
# SBOMs land in /dist/sbom/, already covered by /dist/ above.
/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md

# Pinned CI tooling (installed by `make tools` / `make tools-e2e`)
/.tools/

# Codacy scratch artifacts (the tuning skill's intermediates + run summary).
# .codacy.yaml (Cloud file-exclusions) and .codacy/codacy.config.json (local analysis
# config) ARE tracked; these two are throwaway.
/.codacy/tmp/
/.codacy/configure-codacy-summary.json

# Go
/vendor/
go.work
go.work.sum

# Secrets / local config (never commit credentials or per-env config)
.env
*.env
config.local.*
*.local.yaml
*.secret.*
# the real banned-term list (see scripts/forbidden-words.local.example)
scripts/forbidden-words.local

# Scratch: specs, plans, brainstorming drafts — persist on disk, never enter git history
docs/superpowers/

# Claude Code repo-local config. `settings.json` and `hooks/` ARE tracked — they enforce the
# Backlog.md rules (bare --notes/--plan silently replaces a section; hand-edited task markdown
# loses one at exit 0) for anyone working in this repo. Everything else under .claude/ is
# per-machine state: worktrees, scheduler locks, settings.local.json.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# gcx dashboard snapshot PNGs (scratch)
/snapshots/

# Zensical docs-site build output
/site/

# Injected by the m7kni.io hub at build time — never commit these.
# The hub copies its own SEO template, brand stylesheet and fonts into a clone
# and generates zensical.toml from docs.toml. A tracked copy here is drift, and
# is exactly what the manifest model exists to prevent.
/zensical.toml
docs/overrides/
docs/stylesheets/brand.css
docs/assets/project-icon.svg
docs/assets/project-icon-solid.svg
docs/assets/social-card.png
docs/assets/social-card.svg
docs/fonts/
